          <msContents>
            <summary> A well-written, comprehensive book of medicines and recipes.
              On the title-page is a blazoned coat of arms, gules a cross argent. There is also the following written with red and black ink, and also crossed out: 
              "Item diss Büch Ist Hanns Brümmers / Von Rotwil und ist geschriben / worden Im Jar 1548." which translates to "This book belongs to Hanns Brümmer of Rottweil and was written in the year 1548."
              Then by a different hand: "Urin dem schriber, dreck dem lesser // Von Ainer [?] Wolffgang Wippler // O wie fro ich was / Do ich schrib deo gratias. Fol. 118 Laus deo Von ich wolff / gang Wippler nit gur geschriben / So hon ich aber die wyl vertriben / 1548. "
            </summary>
            <textLang mainLang="de" source="IANA">German</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_158_1">
              <author>Wippler, Wolffgang, fl.1548</author>
              <title type="original" xml:lang="de">Arzneibuch</title>
              <title type="standard" xml:lang="en">Pharmacopoeia</title>
              <textLang mainLang="de" source="IANA">German</textLang>
              <filiation></filiation>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
